{% extends 'help/_layout.html.twig' %}
{% block help_title %}Logging a Meal{% endblock %}

{% block help_body %}
<figure class="figure d-block border rounded shadow-sm overflow-hidden mb-4 w-100">
    <img src="{{ asset('images/help/log-meal.png') }}" class="figure-img img-fluid mb-0 w-100"
         alt="The Log a Meal screen — pick a meal type, add a photo, and add optional notes">
</figure>
<p>Logging a meal is the heart of {{ brand.name }}: take a photo, let the AI estimate what's in it, then confirm and
adjust before saving. You never type in calories by hand.</p>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Step by step</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Tap <strong>Log</strong> and choose or take a photo of your meal.</li>
    <li>{{ brand.name }}'s AI analyzes the photo and estimates calories, macros, a full panel of vitamins and
        minerals, and the ingredients it sees — along with how confident it is.</li>
    <li>On the <strong>Confirm &amp; Refine</strong> screen, review the estimate. Set <strong>"how many servings
        did you eat?"</strong> — the portion control scales the whole estimate up or down.</li>
    <li>If the date isn't today (the app uses your photo's timestamp so you can log a few days of meals at
        once), you'll see a clear notice — adjust the date/time if needed.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Save to log</strong>. You can also <strong>Save &amp; add to favorites</strong> to reuse
        the meal later.</li>
</ol>

<h2 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">If the estimate looks off</h2>
<p>While the AI is still unsure, you can <strong>re-analyze with corrections</strong> (fix an ingredient or
answer its questions) or <strong>attach a second photo</strong> — for example, the nutrition-facts label.
Adding a label usually sharpens the estimate a lot. What you review is exactly what gets saved.</p>

<p class="text-muted small">{{ brand.name }} flags a likely <strong>duplicate</strong> if the same photo is already
logged at the same time, so you don't double-count a meal.</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block help_related %}
<hr class="my-4">
<p class="small text-muted mb-1">Related:</p>
<ul class="small">
    <li><a href="{{ path('app_help_show', {topic: 'favorites'}) }}">Favorite Meals</a></li>
    <li><a href="{{ path('app_help_show', {topic: 'inflammation'}) }}">Inflammation Score</a></li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}
